---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import DashboardExample from "../components/DashboardExample.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../components/InstallCommand.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="SwarmForge — Give every agent a workspace."
  description="Coordinate coding agents in isolated virtual machines. Track their work, preserve their outputs, and bring results back to your project."
  copyControls
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> OPEN SOURCE AGENT INFRASTRUCTURE</p>
        <h1>Give every agent<br>a workspace.<br><span>Keep the whole<br>team in view.</span></h1>
        <p class="intro">Run coding agents in isolated virtual machines. Coordinate their tasks, see their progress, and bring the results back to your project.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/#install">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/GavinGeizer/swarmforge-oss">Explore the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <p class="small muted">Self-hosted control plane · Linux x64 · MCP interface</p>
      </div>
      <DashboardExample />
    </section>
    <section class="install-strip wrap" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">START IN YOUR TERMINAL</p><h2 id="install-heading">One command. Your infrastructure.</h2><p>Install the CLI, configure your providers, and check local readiness.</p></div>
      <InstallCommand />
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">FROM ASSIGNMENT TO HANDOFF</p><h2 id="workflow-heading">A clear path through<br>parallel work.</h2><p>Agents get room to work. You get the controls to understand what happened.</p></div>
      <div class="steps-grid">
        <article class="step"><span class="step-number">01 / ASSIGN</span><h3>Give the task a home.</h3><p>Queue a worker through MCP with its task, instructions, timeout, and expected deliverables. Each worker runs in an isolated VM.</p></article>
        <article class="step"><span class="step-number">02 / OBSERVE</span><h3>See work as it moves.</h3><p>Inspect response activity, results, reported test outcomes, and measured token usage. Find workers with dashboard search and filters.</p></article>
        <article class="step"><span class="step-number">03 / COLLECT</span><h3>Keep what matters.</h3><p>Preserve artifacts, download them with checksum verification, inspect Git handoffs, and clean up eligible retained VMs.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="features-heading"><div class="wrap feature-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">BUILT FOR THE OPERATOR</p><h2 id="features-heading">Control you can<br>actually use.</h2><p>SwarmForge connects your existing tools through a durable control plane you run yourself.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Read the setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <article><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><h3>MCP-native coordination</h3><p>Spawn workers, send follow-up messages, and inspect results from an MCP client.</p></div></article>
        <article><span aria-hidden="true">▤</span><div><h3>Durable results and artifacts</h3><p>Read bounded text directly. Save complete files through authenticated, verified downloads.</p></div></article>
        <article><span aria-hidden="true">◎</span><div><h3>Visible usage and cleanup</h3><p>Configure cost estimates and budget alerts. Preview retention policies before enabling automatic expiry.</p></div></article>
        <article><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span><div><h3>Recovery with context</h3><p>Inspect failure guidance and preservation state, then choose the appropriate next action.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section wrap closing"><p class="eyebrow">BUILD IN THE OPEN</p><h2>Your next agent team<br>starts with a task.</h2><p>Explore the code, try a real workflow, and help shape what comes next.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/">Set up SwarmForge <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/GavinGeizer/swarmforge-oss/issues">Share feedback <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
